# Chalice of the Void, X = 1: {X}{X} is two mana (its ruling), and it enters with one charge counter (CR 614.1c). "Whenever
# a player casts a spell with mana value equal to the number of charge counters on this artifact, counter that spell": its
# controller's own Lightning Bolt (mana value 1) is countered - the trigger goes on the stack above it - and so is Bot2's on
# turn 2, but Bot2's Mind Stone (mana value 2) is not.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Chalice of the Void
Lightning Bolt
Mountain
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Lightning Bolt
Mind Stone
Mountain x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chalice of the Void.Cast(X: 1)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Chalice of the Void.Counters.Charge = 1
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
? Stack = Chalice of the Void; Lightning Bolt
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Choose(Close mana window)
? Stack = Chalice of the Void; Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Mind Stone.Cast

[Expect]
Turn = 2
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Battlefield = Mountain; Mox Ruby; Mox Jet; Mind Stone
Bot1.Battlefield.Chalice of the Void.Counters.Charge = 1
